# A defining tree for the stage-zero representatives

Each row stores an earlier parent, a generator index and an ambient point.
The tree was obtained by breadth-first search using the inverse actions of
`aPerm` and `bPerm`, so inverse tree words give the left representatives required
by `PositiveTable`. These constants alone assert no orbit or stabilizer theorem.
`Representatives` kernel-checks every parent step and every nonroot label.

Source: ATLAS F24G1-p306936B0, GLS3 Table 5.3v and the literal first-four model.
Reproduce with `StageZero/source/representatives.py`.
-/

